1
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,579
Seven minutes late. As always.

2
00:00:19,149 --> 00:00:20,917
Right on time.

3
00:00:23,287 --> 00:00:28,441
I saw nothing. I was asleep. Magnificently asleep.

4
00:00:48,611 --> 00:00:51,662
Morning, Biscuit! Anything exciting happen last night?

5
00:00:51,832 --> 00:00:56,319
Absolutely nothing. Also, check the mailbox. For no reason.

6
00:01:01,389 --> 00:01:06,207
Postmarked... Saturday? Today's Wednesday.

7
00:01:12,377 --> 00:01:16,859
That's my handwriting. That's not normal. That's not even a LITTLE normal.

8
00:01:19,029 --> 00:01:22,086
Theo! You're staring at a mailbox again.

9
00:01:22,256 --> 00:01:26,232
June. I got a letter. From me. From SATURDAY.

10
00:01:26,402 --> 00:01:30,775
Okay. Plan first, panic later. Let me see.

11
00:01:31,545 --> 00:01:36,982
The postmark's real. The ink is dry. And the paper is... warm?

12
00:01:37,152 --> 00:01:39,283
Okay. That's new.

13
00:01:39,453 --> 00:01:40,910
Hold it up. I need proof.

14
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:50,549
Look! In the photo it's glowing. Like an arrow. Pointing at the old Lumen Mill.

15
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:53,165
The letter says bring Dot.

16
00:01:53,335 --> 00:01:57,708
Then we go see the one person in town who can scan a letter from the future.

17
00:01:57,878 --> 00:01:59,802
And who might also have breakfast.

18
00:02:00,572 --> 00:02:04,949
Stand back! Glitch Sniffer Mark Seven is about to make history!

19
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:10,161
Technically... that was a success.

20
00:02:10,331 --> 00:02:13,042
Dot. What was it supposed to do?

21
00:02:13,212 --> 00:02:17,441
Sniff glitches! Find anything in town that flickers when it shouldn't.

22
00:02:17,611 --> 00:02:18,382
Like this?

23
00:02:19,552 --> 00:02:27,566
Whoa, whoa, whoa! This reading is off the chart. Literally. It went off the chart and onto the table!

24
00:02:27,736 --> 00:02:31,803
This letter has the same signal as the pine trees on Flicker nights.

25
00:02:31,974 --> 00:02:34,616
It says, don't let them turn off the Lantern.

26
00:02:34,786 --> 00:02:37,085
Wait. Look at your board, Dot.

27
00:02:41,455 --> 00:02:46,439
Lumen Mill. Demolition on Saturday. The same day as the postmark.

28
00:02:46,609 --> 00:02:53,480
The Lantern in the mill tower. It's been burning since eighteen eighty-seven. With no electricity.

29
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:57,151
So if they knock down the mill... the Lantern goes out.

30
00:02:57,321 --> 00:03:02,371
And something happens. Something big enough that Saturday-Theo wrote himself a letter.

31
00:03:02,541 --> 00:03:04,922
I would like to formally vote for staying here.

32
00:03:05,092 --> 00:03:09,790
Motion denied! You're coming, Biscuit. I upgraded your collar.

33
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,189
That is precisely what frightens me.

34
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:15,802
Sandwich for the road? It's spinach. Mostly.

35
00:03:15,972 --> 00:03:18,577
Nope. Future me said no green sandwiches.

36
00:03:18,747 --> 00:03:21,876
Future you is a coward. I accept.

37
00:03:22,046 --> 00:03:27,004
Okay. Okay, okay, okay. We go to the mill. Tonight. Before Saturday.

38
00:03:27,174 --> 00:03:31,603
Plan first. Flashlights. Compass. Snacks.

39
00:03:31,773 --> 00:03:33,515
And the Sniffer!

40
00:03:35,485 --> 00:03:40,140
So why does everyone call it the Lumen Mill? Was Lumen a person?

41
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:46,299
Ada Lumen. A lantern maker. Mister Hollis at the library told me the whole story.

42
00:03:46,469 --> 00:03:54,376
In eighteen eighty-seven, something fell out of the sky and landed in Mirror Lake. Ada found a glowing stone on the shore.

43
00:03:54,546 --> 00:03:56,726
And she built a lantern factory around it.

44
00:03:56,896 --> 00:04:02,010
Lanterns that never went out. The whole town grew up around their light.

45
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,298
And then what?

46
00:04:03,468 --> 00:04:11,279
In nineteen thirty-one, she closed the factory... and disappeared. People say she left one last message.

47
00:04:11,449 --> 00:04:12,298
What did it say?

48
00:04:12,468 --> 00:04:15,256
Nobody knows. It was never found.

49
00:04:17,026 --> 00:04:19,216
Guys. The trees.

50
00:04:19,387 --> 00:04:22,672
The Flicker. It never starts this early.

51
00:04:22,842 --> 00:04:25,005
SQUIRREL. Squirrel! SQUIRREL!

52
00:04:25,175 --> 00:04:27,704
Ooh. Your collar's picking up interference.

53
00:04:27,874 --> 00:04:31,574
That was not interference. That was a very large squirrel.

54
00:04:31,744 --> 00:04:34,122
Come on. The mill is just past the ridge.

55
00:04:42,892 --> 00:04:46,969
My compass is pointing at the tower. Compasses don't do that.

56
00:04:47,139 --> 00:04:49,071
Today, apparently, they do.

57
00:04:49,241 --> 00:04:54,429
I shall bravely guard the back. Of the group. The very far back.

58
00:04:56,099 --> 00:04:58,615
Did you see that? Someone's up there.

59
00:04:58,785 --> 00:05:00,826
Stay together. I go first.

60
00:05:06,296 --> 00:05:07,831
It's beautiful.

61
00:05:08,001 --> 00:05:09,465
The Lantern.

62
00:05:11,835 --> 00:05:13,723
The stairs! They're glitching!

63
00:05:13,893 --> 00:05:16,369
It's getting weaker. Like it knows what's coming.

64
00:05:17,539 --> 00:05:19,698
There's a plaque. Hold on.

65
00:05:21,068 --> 00:05:26,012
Keep one light burning, and the Pines will remember the way home. A. L.

66
00:05:27,182 --> 00:05:28,953
A. L.? Like Ada Lumen?

67
00:05:33,423 --> 00:05:41,333
Golden threads. From the Lantern to every house in town. If it goes out, the whole town forgets the way home.

68
00:05:41,503 --> 00:05:44,513
I can fix this! Probably! Maybe!

69
00:05:44,683 --> 00:05:52,323
The Sniffer pulls the glitches out. But if I flip it backwards... it pushes light IN.

70
00:05:52,493 --> 00:05:53,605
Is that safe?

71
00:05:53,775 --> 00:05:55,607
Technically!

72
00:05:55,777 --> 00:05:56,315
Do it.

73
00:05:57,685 --> 00:06:00,893
Wrong way! Wrong way! It's sucking the light OUT!

74
00:06:01,063 --> 00:06:03,765
Dot! Your switch. It's upside down!

75
00:06:03,935 --> 00:06:09,551
Oh. Ohhh. Who labeled this? ...I labeled this.

76
00:06:16,121 --> 00:06:20,217
Is it over? Did we win? I would like a sandwich.

77
00:06:21,187 --> 00:06:30,716
June. There's an envelope here. Blank. And a stamp that says... Saturday.

78
00:06:30,886 --> 00:06:34,407
The letter. Theo, you have to write it.

79
00:06:34,577 --> 00:06:37,728
If I don't write it, I never get it. And we never come here.

80
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:43,229
Time loops! I love time loops! I hate time loops! Write it!

81
00:06:46,399 --> 00:06:48,764
Right on time, Mister Bramble.

82
00:06:49,734 --> 00:06:51,348
Who... who are you?

83
00:06:51,518 --> 00:06:52,697
Just the mail.

84
00:06:57,767 --> 00:07:04,692
Mayor Pruitt canceled the demolition. Mister Hollis showed him the plaque. The mill is a historic landmark now.

85
00:07:04,862 --> 00:07:07,880
And Mark Seven is a historic invention.

86
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:10,863
We still don't know who he is. The Night Courier.

87
00:07:11,033 --> 00:07:13,275
Or why his bag said A. L.

88
00:07:13,445 --> 00:07:15,943
Or why nobody has given me a sandwich all week.

89
00:07:21,713 --> 00:07:28,419
Theo. This one's for me. And it's postmarked... eighteen eighty-seven.

90
00:07:28,589 --> 00:07:31,154
Okay. Okay, okay, okay.

91
00:07:34,024 --> 00:07:41,150
Next time on Pixel Pines... my shadow runs away from home. Frankly, I do not blame it.
